course: dictionary
lesson: 6680
title: The oboe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oboe is a woodwind instrument shaped like a long, thin tube. You play it by blowing through a double reed, which makes a clear, slightly sharp sound.
explain: The oboe belongs to the woodwind family of the orchestra, with the flute, clarinet and bassoon. A person who plays it is an oboist, or you can say «oboe player».
explain: Context helps again: «Picture walking into a concert hall: everyone is screeching and tooting at once; that is not the music but tuning up.» The oboe plays the note A, everyone matches it, and then the noise stops.
fact: An oboe is a woodwind instrument shaped like a long, thin tube.
fact: You play an oboe by blowing through a double reed.
fact: The oboe makes a clear, slightly sharp sound.
fact: Before an orchestra plays, the oboe gives the note A and everyone tunes to it.
fact: In «Peter and the Wolf», the oboe plays the duck.
exercise: What family of instruments is the oboe in? | Strings | Percussion | Brass | *Woodwind
exercise: «Before an orchestra plays, the players tune up: usually the oboe plays the note A.» Which note does the oboe usually play? | B | *A | G | C
exercise: How do you play an oboe? | Hit it with sticks | Pluck the strings with your fingers | Shake it hard | *Blow through a double reed
test: In «Peter and the Wolf», which instrument plays the duck? | *Oboe | Flute | Violin | Drum
test: What is a person who plays the oboe called? | A conductor | A drummer | A tuba player | *An oboist
exam: Why does everyone match the oboe's note before a concert? | *So everyone plays in tune together | So the concert starts late | Because the oboe is the loudest instrument | To show off
